# Skeletons match the screen

When a shipped screen has a loading state, the skeleton must look like that screen — same chrome, same blocks, same row shape. Not two generic bars.

## Do

- Keep the screen title, back and menu buttons, search field, and section headings as the real controls while data loads. Skeleton only the values the query fills.
- Mirror the rows the user will see when data arrives: the same picture size and shape (posters stay 2:3, episode pictures 16:9), the same number of text lines, and the tick circle where a tick goes.
- Use the same outer padding and column tracks as the loaded page.
- Follow `docs/product/product-requirements.md`: loading uses skeletons matching the real layout.

## Do not

- Ship a skeleton that is only a couple of full-width bars or a blank pulse box.
- Use a spinner-only full page for a list screen.
- Replace a whole screen with a skeleton when its header and buttons are already known.
- Copy another screen’s skeleton when this screen’s layout is different.

Up next, Upcoming, Discover, and My shows are the bar for this app.
